# Brand, writing and audit work package

This package adds the selected brand guidance and a complete writing guide, then uses those rules to audit the design system. The follow-up remediation phase implements the findings and expands complete component examples and native task specifications. Its checklist records the evidence separately from the original review.

## Read the deliverables

- [Design styles](../styles/index.html): colour, typography, data and illustration.
- [Writing for home automation](../content/index.html): ten chapters, household examples and testable rules.
- [Whole-system audit](design-system-audit.html): confirmed findings, evidence and acceptance criteria.
- [Component organisation](component-audit.html): canonical families, duplication and stable-URL implementation.
- [Home Assistant specification coverage](missing-components.html): 30 dedicated guides, existing native capability and implementation boundaries.

The [remediation verification record](../reference/remediation-verification.json) records executed checks, browser observations and publication status. The [machine-readable checklist](../reference/guidance-work-package.json) supplies the records below. A completed checklist item has evidence. An audit finding remains open until its proposed remedy meets the recorded acceptance criteria.

For subsequent changes, use the [brand rule checklist](../reference/brand-guidance-checklist.json), [writing review checklist](../reference/writing-guide-checklist.json) and [component audit checklist](../reference/component-audit-checklist.json). The writing checklist is a reusable blank template. The brand checklist separates completed source and documentation review from interface checks that still need implementation evidence. Their scope remains separate from the named remediation checks below.

